  "source": "Carlo Gavazzi WM14 Advanced / CPT-DIN Advanced Communication Protocol, version 2 revision 2 (9 January 2008)",
  "notes": [
    "Carlo Gavazzi WM14 Advanced and CPT-DIN Advanced (WM14 revision 5 and later, CPT-DIN revision 6 and later).",
    "Floats are IEEE 754 with the low word first (the manual's byte order is bits 15-8, 7-0, 31-24, 23-16), so the map uses word_order little. 32-bit integers are also low word first.",
    "The same values can be read with function 03 or 04; at most 12 registers per request. Optional RS485 port: 8N1, 4800 to 38400 baud, address 1 to 255.",
    "Energy counters are in tenths of kWh / kvarh; the hour counter is in hundredths of an hour.",
    "Not tested on a device. The settings (programming) tables of the manual are not in this map."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
